# Line coverage, ratcheted. This number may go UP, never down.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-19 at adoption: 64.76% lines, 65.01% regions, 70.80%
# functions (R50). The floor starts AT the measurement rather than at a
# target, because a gate nobody can pay down gets bypassed -- which is .:B6,
# and which the clippy ratchet already avoided by measuring 290 violations
# before choosing a strategy.
#
# 98% is the DESTINATION, recorded in §C. This is the route.
#
# A percentage cannot tell a test that ASSERTS behaviour from one that merely
# EXECUTES lines. `src/review:negative_only` exists because a detector was
# tested only on the empty case and a function returning `Vec::new()` passed.
# Raising this number rewards that shape, so it is the SECOND layer: T89's
# pub-fn pairing check is the first.
#
# By node at adoption -- `cli` is the lever, at 445 uncovered lines:
#   code 98.3 · lens 94.5 · spec 92.5 · tokens 88.9 · state 88.0 · fed 87.1
#   ollama 70.9 · tdd 69.0 · plan 66.5 · slice 63.6 · review 63.0
#   land 55.2 · assay 54.0 · cli 0.0
lines 90.07
#
# MEASUREMENT VARIANCE, observed rather than assumed: two runs of the same
# tree reported 71.27% and 71.17%. Three later runs all reported 71.17%. The
# floor is the LOW observation. If this gate ever flaps, the fix is a STATED
# margin in the comparison -- not a quietly lowered floor, which would hide
# the drift this file exists to catch.
#
# THE MARGIN WAS 0.3, and it is GONE as of 2026-08-21. Its cause was named
# here on 2026-08-19: the suite was not hermetic. `.bbx-state` lives in the
# repo, tests both READ and WROTE it, and `derived_prefill` branches on its
# contents -- so which lines executed depended on what previous runs left
# behind. Measured spread 75.26-75.35.
#
# `src/ollama:T13` is CLOSED and the margin came out with it. The fix is not
# T13's original `BBX_STATE` plan -- an env var is process-global, so parallel
# tests would still share it, and `set_var` is unsafe under edition 2024 while
# this crate forbids unsafe. What landed instead:
#
#   * every store-touching fn has a `*_in(&mut State, ..)` core, so a test
#     brings its own store (`src/plan`, `src/ollama`);
#   * `generate_via` SPLIT into `stream` (measures) and `learn_from`
#     (persists), because a fn that ends by writing what it observed cannot be
#     exercised without mutating shared state (`src/ollama:V20`, `B9`);
#   * a `Transport` declares whether its timings are REAL, and a double says
#     no -- so a scripted reply never teaches the pace model that calls take
#     no time.
#
# VERIFIED: `cargo test` leaves `.bbx-state` byte-identical, and two
# consecutive `cargo llvm-cov` runs report the same number to the digit.
#
# DROP RECORDED 2026-08-19, 75.50% -> 75.11%, with the reason this file asks
# for rather than a silent edit.
#
# CAUSE, and it is structural: the assay node's experiments are `#[ignore]`d
# -- they only run against a live endpoint -- and because this repo puts tests
# INLINE, an ignored body counts in the denominator while never executing.
# Their endpoint-only helpers are uncoverable for the same reason. So every
# experiment added to `src/assay` lowers this number, and the better the
# instrument gets the worse the percentage reads.
#
# That is a measurement artefact, not a regression: no line stopped being
# covered. `.:T96` is the fix -- move the ignored titrations to `tests/`,
# where they are a separate target and stop counting against lib coverage.
# Estimated recovery ~130 lines, roughly +3 points, after which this stops
# recurring on every experiment.
#
# THIRD DROP, 75.11% -> 74.75%, same structural cause, recorded rather than
# fixed because the fix is a refactor and this was written unattended.
#
# Three drops for one reason is no longer a note, it is evidence: every
# experiment added to `src/assay` LOWERS this number, because an `#[ignore]`d
# body counts in the denominator and never runs. T82, T83, the mutation sweep
# and T84 each cost ~0.4 points while each made the instrument better.
#
# `.:T96` is the fix and it should come BEFORE the next experiment, or this
# file becomes a log of excuses. Estimated recovery ~170 lines, roughly +3
# points, and it stops recurring.
#
# FIRST EXPERIMENT THAT DID NOT COST A POINT, 74.75% -> 75.39%, measured
# 2026-08-20 (T97, the ambiguity detector).
#
# Its live runner went into `tests/ambiguity.rs` instead of inline, and the
# per-file table CONFIRMS what `.:T96` predicted: `tests/ambiguity.rs` does
# not appear in the report at all, so its `#[ignore]`d body is outside the
# denominator. `assay/mod.rs` rose 57.55% -> 64.74% on the deterministic half
# alone.
#
# So T96's estimate is now measured rather than assumed, and the rule for the
# experiments after this one is: the endpoint-only runner goes in `tests/`,
# the mechanical half stays inline where it is covered.
#
# THE THREE DROPS ARE PAID BACK, 75.84% -> 79.28%, measured 2026-08-21 (T96).
#
# All eight `#[ignore]`d titrations moved out of `src/assay` inline tests into
# integration targets: tests/{blind_lens,generation,authorship,mutants,
# signature}.rs, joining tests/ambiguity.rs. `src/assay` went 67.00% -> 91.75%
# and its missed lines 264 -> 48.
#
# ESTIMATE vs MEASUREMENT: this file predicted "~170 lines, roughly +3
# points". Measured +3.44. The estimate was sound and the fix was deferred
# four times anyway.
#
# What made it more than a move: each titration's REPORT was a `fn` that
# printed and returned nothing, so its only test called it and asserted
# NOTHING -- executing lines while proving none of them, which is the exact
# shape this file warns about two paragraphs up. The reports are now `pub fn`
# returning `String`, unit-tested on their content, and the endpoint half
# lives in `tests/`. Nothing is written twice (`src/fed:B13`).
#
# So the number rose for two different reasons and only one of them is
# denominator arithmetic. The other is tests that now assert.
